    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "49990b429ddc07efe2dad72ae6bbc1c24bbc79e3f9a22444b43c5c5e4ddb9513",
      "text": "Private charter back to the mainland, ~5.5 hours\n\nIn the morning — an excursion to Ahu Akivi, the only platform on the island where seven moai face the ocean: according to legend, they represent the seven explorers sent by King Hotu Matu'a in search of new land. Next, the Puna Pau quarry, source of the red scoria used for the moai's topknots, and the Tahai ceremonial complex with its restored platforms, including Ko Te Riku — the only statue with restored eyes. From Easter Island, the only route back is through Santiago — there are no direct flights to the north of the country from here. Return by private charter and an overnight in the capital before the next flight deep into the desert.\n\n•  Santiago (1 night): The Singular Santiago, Lastarria Room, BB",
